  "id": "DbYnLlBM1-z",
  "title": "Video by linusoyugi",
  "description": "Feminism didn’t primarily liberate the average woman.\nIt primarily enriched a tiny minority of men.\nExpanding women’s paid work increased the labor supply.\nThat put downward pressure on wages and weakened workers’ bargaining power.\nThe biggest winners? Capitalists — mostly men — who got a larger, cheaper workforce.\nSex-positivity messaging framed casual sex as empowerment.\nIt increased the supply of short-term sex.\nMen (on average higher in sociosexuality) benefit far more from this than women do.\nThe orgasm gap in casual sex makes that clear: men 80–90%, women 30–40%.\nSo the real beneficiaries of modern feminism aren’t most women.\nThey’re a small group of already-powerful or highly promiscuous men.\nTechnology and individual-rights ideas did the heavy lifting for women’s actual freedom.\nFeminism just handed extra advantages to the few at the top.\n\n#Feminism\n#GenderDebate\n#SexPositivity\n#CasualSex\n#orgasmgap",
